conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6759308Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6768839Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6847431Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6855434Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6855732Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6856174Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6856376Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6856549Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6856971Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6857261Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6857442Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6857798Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6857992Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6858609Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6859108Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6859513Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6859720Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6859915Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6860024Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6860193Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6860306Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6860520Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6860826Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6860920Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6861104Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6861322Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6861590Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6868417Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6868595Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6868732Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6868843Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6869081Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6869370Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6869710Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6869970Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6870300Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6870577Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6870853Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6881908Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6882460Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6892507Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6892928Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6893090Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6894276Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6894661Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6909567Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6910020Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6918323Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6918819Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6919100Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6919272Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6919424Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6919618Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6919778Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6920104Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6920287Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6920377Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6920607Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6920763Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6920949Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6921330Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:24.6921509Z 
