conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5091081Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5101937Z ^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5102653Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5103192Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5103443Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5104030Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5105025Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5105606Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5105983Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5106949Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5107304Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5108277Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5109200Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5109737Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5110152Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5110530Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5110739Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5111017Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5111249Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5111681Z    can use Nix.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5111830Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5111970Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5112168Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5112595Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5113096Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5115579Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5115797Z I will:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5116167Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5116545Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5119247Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5119780Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5120227Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5120547Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5120915Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5121440Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5122183Z    /root
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5133092Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5134110Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5146103Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:32.5146689Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
