conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3504018Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3504371Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3505109Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3505522Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3505880Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3507482Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3507892Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3508470Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3509356Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3510300Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3511247Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3511639Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3512002Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3512433Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3512754Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3513457Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3513760Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3513978Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3514305Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3514857Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3515880Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3516657Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3516939Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3517179Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3517676Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3518371Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3519115Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3519910Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3520476Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3521117Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3521818Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3522596Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3531701Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3533416Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3542627Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3543873Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3544311Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3544787Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3545678Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3564931Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3575036Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3576612Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3577604Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3578359Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3578794Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3579159Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3579594Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3579948Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3580759Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3581167Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3581392Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3581982Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3582380Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3582711Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3583457Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3583720Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3583811Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3584369Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3585529Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:40.3586589Z been installed on this system.
